cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: Panopticon
abstract: >-
  Hardware-triggered multi-camera video acquisition for 3D animal pose
  estimation. One TTL trigger fires every camera, the frames are encoded to
  H.264 on the GPU during the recording, and each camera's video keeps only
  the triggers every camera captured, matched by the frame's block ID, so the
  videos are aligned trigger for trigger. The same application records and
  solves a ChArUco calibration and runs optogenetic stimulation from the
  trigger board.
